# Fetch AI Smart Contract Audit Report

## Overview

This folder contains a public smart contract audit report for **Fetch.ai**, one of the most recognized projects at the intersection of artificial intelligence, autonomous agents, and blockchain infrastructure.

Softstack audited the **Fetch.ai Agentverse Launchpad** smart contracts, providing security review support for infrastructure tied to the broader Fetch.ai ecosystem. As Fetch.ai has evolved into a central pillar of the **Artificial Superintelligence Alliance**, this audit is a strong public reference for security work connected to one of the most ambitious decentralized AI ecosystems in the industry.

## About Fetch.ai

**Fetch.ai** is a blockchain and AI infrastructure project focused on autonomous agents, decentralized machine learning systems, and agent-based digital economies.

The project has become especially important through its role in the **Artificial Superintelligence Alliance**, alongside SingularityNET and CUDOS. This places Fetch.ai at the center of one of the most visible attempts to build decentralized infrastructure for advanced AI applications.

## Why This Project Matters

Fetch.ai is far more than a standard token project. It is part of a broader push to build the infrastructure layer for decentralized AI, autonomous coordination, and agent-based applications.

That makes this audit a strong public reference for:

- smart contract security for AI and agent ecosystems
- launchpad and ecosystem infrastructure audits
- security work for large-scale blockchain and AI projects
- Web3 security supporting next-generation protocol infrastructure

For founders, buyers, and technical teams, this is a particularly strong proof point because Fetch.ai combines high technical ambition with broad market visibility.

## ASI Vision and ASI:Chain Relevance

Fetch.ai is now part of the **Artificial Superintelligence Alliance**, a major decentralized AI initiative formed to unify infrastructure, token economics, and ecosystem development across leading AI-native crypto projects.

As part of that broader vision, the alliance has announced and launched early phases of **ASI:Chain**, a Layer 1 blockchain designed specifically for advanced decentralized AI applications. This significantly increases the strategic importance of the Fetch.ai ecosystem and strengthens the value of any public security work tied to its infrastructure.

That makes this audit relevant not only as a standalone smart contract review, but also as a public security reference connected to one of the most ambitious decentralized AI infrastructure initiatives in Web3.

